A||||10||Slick781||mod help||||1||
Z||000000||Slick781||03-25-2001||09:08 PM||||alright, ill be askin quite a few questions on here again... since we just bought an 85 gt as a project car.....<P>we have the interior completely stripped out, and most the panels off of the car... <P>we've been thinkin about what all to do to it, so my first question is - what all should i be thinking about while the interior is stripped... the one thing that pops in my head is the speaker behind the seat mod...<P>basically im just lookin for as many things as you guys can think about :-)<P>thanx,<BR>david||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||03-25-2001||10:41 PM||||Well, if you want some power options, now'd be a good time to add them.  Ive added power locks, mirrors, trunk release and a peformance sound system.  I already had power windows, so a big relief there.  If you dont have power windows and you want them, just get a door with everything in it already, the locks are easy but the windows (i've heard) are a real pain to try to install.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||Slick781||03-26-2001||11:54 PM||||yep, we've got all that stuff... thankfully...<P>anybody else have any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||03-27-2001||01:50 AM||||definately upgrade the speakers. and if the dash is cracked, it would be a good idea to fix that. fix all the warped pieces, if any. and you could even paint your interior. should be pretty easy with everything out. also, clean up the carpet while everything's out of your way. a nice, clean, stain-free interior looks really sharp. you could get the door windows and rear window tinted.<P>that's about all i can think of for now.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Taijiguy||03-27-2001||09:30 AM||||When you put it back together, devise as many ways as you can think of to secure the dash more solidly, and to try and insulate it against rattles and squeeks. I haven't done this yet, but it's absolutely in my 85's future. On a bumpy road it's the biggest rattle bucket I've ever been in. I'm not exactly sure where I would start, having never pulled the dash out, but I would expend the most brain-power to that end. Also some of that expanding foam stuff from a can squirted in some strategic places to improve air and sound insulation comes to mind. (and it's easily shaped when it sets up. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tigger||03-27-2001||11:00 AM||||Good time to fix rust, especially around those drain plugs under the seats.  Another thing to look at is to replace your battery tray.||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||03-27-2001||11:08 AM||||Also, just thought of this.  If you're ebrake cables tend to stick and could stand to be replaced, Do it while the carpet is out.  Should be much easier to feed the cable through the grommet in the fire wall when the carpet is out of the car.<P>If you are thinking of adding a alarm/keyless entry system, do it now while all the wires are availble, and when the dash is out.  You can hide the control unit in a better location way up under the dash.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||03-27-2001||12:56 PM||||Taijiguy--I've had 2 '85 GTs.  Neither one has had any significant squeaks.  Must be your car.||||reg||1
Z||000008||stsmithgt||03-27-2001||03:08 PM||||How about running some wires to go to a couple of seat warmers? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gunhotWHT.gif"> ||||reg||3
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||03-27-2001||06:00 PM||||I'd line the panels with dynamat to cut down on engine and road noise.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||85Josh||03-27-2001||09:14 PM||||Monkeyman, my 150000 mile 85 is also rattle free, except for the !@#$#$%%^ heat stove for the thermac, and Wolfhounds gonna sell me one of those. I fact, it is the quietest high-mileage car I've ever had.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4<BR>CAVALRY SCOUT!(stuck in Field Artillery)||||reg||1
